# Cloudinary Implementation Guide

**Status:** ✅ Fully Implemented  
**Date:** 2026-08-10

---

## Overview

This document describes how Cloudinary is integrated into the Indiyano website — how images are uploaded, stored, optimized, and cleaned up.

---

## How It Works

### Upload Flow

```
Admin UI (ImageUpload component)
    ↓  POST /api/upload (multipart/form-data: file, alt, folder)
    ↓  Auth guard (requireOwner) + Rate limiting (20/min, 200/hr per IP)
    ↓  File validation (type: jpeg/png/webp/gif, size: max 5MB)
    ↓  uploadBufferToCloudinary() in src/lib/cloudinary.ts
    ↓  Cloudinary SDK upload_stream
    ↓  Cloudinary CDN
    ↓  Returns CloudinaryImage object
    ↓  Stored in MongoDB (Product/Banner/Category document)
```

### Folder Structure

Images are organized into an enterprise folder hierarchy on Cloudinary:

```
indiyano/
├── products/            # Product main + gallery images
├── banners/             # Hero carousel banner images
├── categories/          # Category main images
└── subcategories/       # Subcategory images
```

Each upload generates a **unique public_id** (`<timestamp>-<random>`, e.g. `1725840827341-4f8a2c`) to prevent filename collisions. The `overwrite` flag is **not** used.

### Image Optimization

Every image is automatically optimized via transformation presets:

| Preset | Dimensions | Transformations |
|--------|-----------|-----------------|
| `thumbnail` | 300×300 | `c_fill, gravity_auto, f_auto, q_auto` |
| `card` | 500×500 | `c_fill, gravity_auto, f_auto, q_auto` |
| `detail` | 800×800 | `c_fill, gravity_auto, f_auto, q_auto` |
| `zoom` | 1200×1200 | `c_fill, gravity_auto, f_auto, q_auto` |

**Optimization techniques:**
- `f_auto` — serves the best format (WebP/AVIF) based on the browser
- `q_auto` — auto-quality balancing file size and visual fidelity
- `c_fill` — crops to fill the exact dimensions
- `gravity_auto` — subject-aware cropping (keeps faces/important regions)

All four transformation URLs are generated on upload and stored in the `CloudinaryImage` object.

### CloudinaryImage Data Structure

```typescript
{
  publicId: "indiyano/products/1725840827341-4f8a2c",
  url: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../image/upload/...",
  secureUrl: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../image/upload/...",
  width: 800,
  height: 800,
  alt: "Basmati Rice",
  transformations: {
    thumbnail: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../w_300,h_300,c_fill.../...",
    card: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../w_500,h_500,c_fill.../...",
    detail: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../w_800,h_800,c_fill.../...",
    zoom: "https://res.cloudinary.com/.../w_1200,h_1200,c_fill.../..."
  }
}
```

