## Cascade Cleanup (Update & Delete)

### Update (PUT) — Diff-based deletion

When an entity is updated, the system compares old vs new Cloudinary images and deletes only the images that are **no longer referenced**:

```
Old images (from DB)  →  collectPublicIds()
New images (from body) →  collectPublicIds()
toDelete = oldIds - newIds  →  deleteCloudinaryImages(toDelete)
```

**Products:** Compares main image + gallery images.  
**Categories:** Compares main image + all subcategory images.  
**Banners:** Compares the single banner image.

### Delete (DELETE) — Full cascade

When an entity is deleted, **all its Cloudinary images are also deleted**:

| Entity | Images Deleted |
|--------|---------------|
| Product | Main image + all gallery images |
| Category | Main image + all subcategory images |
| Banner | Banner image |

### Failure Handling

- **DB is the source of truth.** If Cloudinary deletion fails, the entity is still updated/deleted (no orphaned DB records).
- Failed deletions are returned as `warnings` in the API response and displayed as amber warning banners in the admin UI.
- A future background job could retry failed deletions.

